summary:
  The heal run forgets its generation number, so a slow reply overwrites a newer one.

history:
  Heal rewrites the user's SAVED station address. Without the generation guard a
  late callback from an abandoned attempt can land after the user already moved
  on and write the wrong URL into their station list. This is the most damaging
  class of bug in the widget: it corrupts saved user data, not just the display.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
    var mySeq = ++_healSeq;

replace:
    var mySeq = _healSeq;

expect:
  tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_heal_generation_is_claimed_fresh_and_abandoned_whole
  — it pins the ++ pre-increment this mutant removes. A behavioural version
  (two heal runs, the first one's late reply must be dropped) does not exist
  yet; it wants the run bookkeeping out of main.qml first.
